                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a5d10eb-e964-4c6e-94e5-ba648105dfb7",
                                                "sense_id": "dad76b35-dcca-39a9-b0cb-35f3ceadc1fd",
                                                "text": "1978, Peter Bailey, Leisure and class in Victorian England: Rational recreation and the contest for control, quoting \"a British observation from early 20th century\", read in Orvar Löfgren, On Holiday: A History of Vacationing (2002) - The excursion train used to vomit forth, at Easter and in Whitsun week, throngs of millhands of the period, cads and their flames, tawdry, blowsy, noisy, drunken."
                                            }
